{"id": "EUVD-2026-76588", "enisaUuid": "438a62fa-67ca-3b0e-b04b-5af9c9bba8fd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: fix stale s2s_cp_stateids IDR entry for async COPY\n\nFor an async COPY, nfsd4_copy() called nfs4_init_copy_state() before\ndup_copy_fields(), so the s2s_cp_stateids IDR was pointed at\n&u->copy->cp_stateid -- memory in the per-rqstp COMPOUND buffer that is\nreused by the next request. dup_copy_fields() copies only the value into\nasync_copy, so the IDR slot dangled at the transient buffer for the whole\nbackground copy. Any IDR walker then dereferences reused request memory:\nthe laundromat reads cs_type from it and, if the bytes look like an\nexpired NFS4_COPYNOTIFY_STID, follows into\nrefcount_dec()/idr_remove()/kfree() on garbage; manage_cpntf_state() has\nthe same exposure via idr_find().\n\nDuplicate the fields first, then register the stateid on the stable\nasync_copy. result->cb_stateid is unchanged.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:16", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdce362f49410b9def65d76c21f6259cd89696d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7aa34ea78f74e6ef60c8112635a87fc43d57f6c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b4e5e9ba5ae13808b8a6d229d87c54611ba0e7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14b978e8d05ce018d0afbeb6611833ef91713a02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0beaee498e11880e72826026db0e9c9890fc114"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gwc7-hc26-hx5g", "CVE-2026-89676"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2e8bd118-23e7-3990-9d58-e316f13f726c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e0639dc5805a9d4faaa2c07ad98fa853b9529dd3 <14b978e8d05ce018d0afbeb6611833ef91713a02"}, {"id": "358556d3-24b7-3a2a-8879-ff4188a17e78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.20"}, {"id": "7133f6b3-7d86-3b0b-9f82-ffc15e95271a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9e85c1f4-6703-3a07-9e72-56d979707812", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e0639dc5805a9d4faaa2c07ad98fa853b9529dd3 <bdce362f49410b9def65d76c21f6259cd89696d8"}, {"id": "a422346c-7ba1-3ef0-b56a-a70e7d6ebed7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "a59caf8b-84be-343f-9064-377aebb4fa2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "c8d9002c-f068-336d-8488-309b3902588b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "c9b842d7-2812-32c9-ade2-4365606d2549", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e0639dc5805a9d4faaa2c07ad98fa853b9529dd3 <7aa34ea78f74e6ef60c8112635a87fc43d57f6c9"}, {"id": "d8552097-40d4-30da-95b1-c8f349b2336d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d8b4d342-f2c3-3deb-9792-f10f4e14e4d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "de316cbd-4d91-32ba-955c-ae1670d3cd66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e0639dc5805a9d4faaa2c07ad98fa853b9529dd3 <9b4e5e9ba5ae13808b8a6d229d87c54611ba0e7a"}, {"id": "f129509f-c7b5-3eea-9a52-40d645856b62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e0639dc5805a9d4faaa2c07ad98fa853b9529dd3 <d0beaee498e11880e72826026db0e9c9890fc114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bc3b5055-ddd8-3fc2-a78f-14b6e2fa9a5e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}